  "summary": "I wrote `src/main.ts` for the blizzard mountain pass. It passes `typecheck`, but I couldn't run `vite build` or open it in a browser, so the visuals and tuning are untested.\n\n- **Terrain:** one procedural heightfield mesh (about 37k vertices) with vertex colours. It has a V-shaped valley that climbs, with white and blue-grey snow, dark rock on steep ground, and a darker packed-snow trail that winds along the valley floor. Distant peaks rise at the far end.\n- **Rocks and poles:** about 200 faceted dark rocks with snow caps, drawn as instances. 18 wooden trail poles with crossbars and snow caps stand on alternating sides of the trail, every 6.5 m.\n- **Cabin:** it sits on a levelled pad beside the trail halfway up, built from boxes. It has log lines, a stepped gable, a two-slab roof with snow, a chimney, and a door. Two orange emissive windows face the trail, each with a warm point light.\n- **Sky and fog:** the sky is a flat pale-grey background colour. The fog uses the same colour at density 0.0075, which should turn the far peaks into soft silhouettes.\n- **Snow:** 4200 flakes in two sizes (3000 small, 1200 large), drawn as wind-angled streak quads by a custom shader that follows the camera. Gusts come from a time function that raises the flake count (about 60% to 100% visible), speed and streak length. At least 1500 flakes stay visible between gusts.\n- **Camera:** it walks the trail at 1.7 m eye height, with a small bob, sway and head turn. It loops every 86 s with a hard cut back to the start.\n- **Page setup:** the canvas isn't resized (`resize: false`). `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after the first frames are drawn.\n- **Camera dependency:** the camera movement relies on `app.camera.setPose`. If the camera controller is missing, the camera would stay still.\n\nThings I could not check without a browser:\n- The roof slab rotation signs are guessed. If they are wrong, the roof shows as an inverted V.\n- The light intensities may leave the snow too bright or too dark.",
